Exercise: Failed Logon Burst


Objective: Generate repeated failed logon attempts on the Windows VM and confirm they are detected in Wazuh.


Command (run on the Windows VM):



for /L %i in (1,1,6) do net use \\127.0.0.1\IPC$ /user:baduser Wrong123


This loop attempts to authenticate six times with an invalid username and password. Bursts of failed logons like this are a core detection use case for a SIEM.


Possible causes of this pattern:


Brute-force attack
Credential stuffing
Password spraying
Misconfigured system or service (e.g., a stale saved credential)


Locating the events in Wazuh:


In the Wazuh Dashboard, select the agent (node) you want to monitor.
Click More, then under Threat Intelligence, select Threat Hunting.
In the search bar, enter the Windows event ID 4625 to filter for failed logons.


Expected results:


Six Windows Event ID 4625 entries (failed logon).
Wazuh rule 60122 (Windows logon failure) firing for each attempt.


Next step(s): Use these results as the baseline for a custom Wazuh rule that escalates repeated failed logons (for example, multiple 4625 events from the same source within a short time window) into a higher-severity alert.
